A||||3||DXR_DAD||Yes, It`s the rear scoop again**
Z||000000||DXR_DAD||08-20-99||08:26 PM||||I got it today. It looks like its going to be simple to install....but do I need to brace or support the lid in some way once I cut the hole in it, and will the lid pop-up with the added weight of the tail & scoop? Then what about the water thing.<p>HELP  before I make the first cut!!!!!
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||08-21-99||01:54 PM||||Here I was, typing a long story about installation of the wing, then I re-read the topic and I noticed you were talking about the <b>scoop</b>! Oh well...
Z||000002||TOM||08-21-99||09:22 PM||||If you look at the under side of the decklid. You will see the big squarish section where the EMI plate is or would be. The next section to the rear is about 6 inches by 23 inches. This smaller one is all I cut out on mine. Careful you cannot go the full 23 inches wide eith the hole. Another buyer also cut out the bigger section as big as the scoop permitted but left the cross brace intact. The deck springs should be strong enough as long as you have the heavy ones for use with the wing. The weight of the scoop is forward. If not the spring postion can be adjusted stiffer. There is a pin where the spring attaches to the car. Forward is weaker,rearward is stronger. Mine does not have the wing and I have not changed to stiffer springs. Any other questions/concerns please dont hesitate to contact me.
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||08-21-99||11:05 PM||||Thanks Tom,  Thats all I needed. I think I got it from here.
